  "query_preview": "..\nA weak cold front passed SE through the CWA overnight with a weak\nsurface high expected to pass east over southern Sask overnight \ntonight.\n\nA fairly large upper low off the California coast will keep an\ninduced ridge to its east, allowing NE MT to experience dry\nconditions and warmer than normal temps through Friday.\n\nBut the upper low will merge with the northern stream jet and move\ninto Montana Friday. This will pull up moisture from the Desert SW\nwhile a surface low developing over the CWA moves to our NE this\nweekend. This will allow NW winds to increase late Friday behind \na cold front. Rain showers behind the cold front will move NE \nacross the western zones. The showers are expected to exit the CWA\nlate Friday night/Saturday with significantly cooler high temps \nSaturday.\n\nRough conditions on Fort Peck Lake can be expected beginning\nFriday afternoon (western portion) through Saturday. Check the\nforecast if you have plans to visit the area later this week.\n\nRainfall amounts still look to be greatest over the NW half of \nthe CWA with the total amount expected less than a half inch.\n\nBeyond Saturday, temps look to remain below normal as an upper\nridge early next week doen't nudge east of the Pac NW.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nLeft what the NBM gave me for weather elements today. As usual,\nconfidence is shaky with rainfall amounts later this week. There\nwas a slight decrease with total rainfall (QPF) for Friday through\nSaturday morning. TFJ",
